                    <div class="modal fade" id="khushabu" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Khushabu Devi</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>Khushabu Devi emerged winner at Aparajita &#8216;Kahaani&#8217; 2024 (now &#8216;Aakar&#8217;). She leads the Pratigya Macchardani Utpadak Samooh, a group of SHG and non-SHG women from three villages in her block. Together, they manufacture mosquito nets, with 14-15 machines at a central location and others working from home. During the pandemic, they fulfilled mask orders, but have since returned to producing mosquito nets. Her group now generates an impressive annual revenue of around Rs. 10 lakh, empowering local women through sustainable&nbsp;livelihoods.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="aradhitaA" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Aradhita Agarwal</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>While women work in multitudes of tea estates, we see very few manage them &#8211; and that&#8217;s the &#8216;tea&#8217; on Director of Operations at Ellenbarrie Tea Co. Ltd. as well as Karala Valley tea estates and the co-owner of Chaika Tea &#8211; the brilliant Aradhita Agarwal!</p>
                    <p>This true star is our 2024 Business &amp; Entrepreneurship winner. A woman who believes in the power of breaking through stereotypes, who believes that to be Aparajita is to believe that you can do anything.</p> 
                    <p>Building on this faith of Aradhita&#8217;s, we&#8217;re proud to announce that we&#8217;ve connected with a professional aiming to equip the female workers on her tea estates with the skill of financial&nbsp;literacy.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="katayunS" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Katayun Saklat</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>Katayun Saklat is the passionate stained glass painter behind Kolkata&#8217;s Fire Temple windows, and the winner of the 2024 Popular Award in the Visual Arts category!</p>
                    <p>She is the founder of Gallery Katayun. With a rich career exploring themes from dreamscapes to Zoroastrianism, she is dedicated to advancing education for deaf children, advocating for the Parsi community, and promoting young artists. As one of India&#8217;s most accomplished stained glass designers, her work is part of several public and private collections &#8211; as such, in supporting our nominees&#8217; dreams in the 13th edition, we are compiling for Katayun a comprehensive memoir&nbsp;of&nbsp;her&nbsp;work!</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="minaP" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Mina Pandit</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>Even the pandemic couldn&#8217;t stop this third-generation street food specialist, the winner of the Popular Award in Gourmet for 2024. She believes in self-sufficiency and hard work, passing on her skills to her 4 daughters, catering to prominent clients such as Rekha and Kapil Dev besides garnering extensive media coverage and the love of Kolkata&#8217;s community street&nbsp;food&nbsp;lovers!</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="ranguS" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Rangu Souriya</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>The force from Siliguri fighting against human trafficking &#8211; founder of Kanchanjungha Uddhar Kendra, Rangu Souriya, won the Popular Award for Community Service &amp; Advocacy in 2024!</p>
                    <p>She founded her NGO in 2004 with her own savings &amp; small donations from well-wishers at a time when the closures of tea gardens were causing spikes in the trafficking of women &amp; children. Her work has earned her numerous honours from both government and non-government&nbsp;organisations.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="madhu" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Madhu Neotia</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>Under her aegis, The Indian Institute of Crafts and Design (IICD) Jaipur has flourished, as has The India Story, a flagship project of the Neotia Arts Trust. In 2010, Madhu took home the Aparajita for Healthcare for making specialised healthcare accessible for women &amp; children through the Bhagirathi Neotia Woman and Child Care Centre, and later joined us as jury member &amp; true steering force for Aparajita. She embodies every Aparajita that has graced our platform.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="anu" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Prof. Anuradha Lohia</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>A recipient of honours like the Stree Shakti Award &amp; the National Award for Young Woman Bioscientist, Smt. Anuradha has gained unparalleled experience as a visiting scientist in several countries. As a woman in STEM herself, she champions the adoption of STEM amongst women &amp; is a passionate supporter of promoting classical dance forms.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="dolly" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Dolly Jain</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>So many tears shed, so many hearts full. Dolly Jain &#8211; a true “parampara ki parchai.”</p>
                                  <p>Gracing the Sanmarg Aparajita stage not for the first time, but as Aparajita’s FIRST EVER undeclared Jury Awardee… And the surprises kept coming because Ruchika Gupta and the Sanmarg Aparajita team worked very hard to secretly bring Dolly’s daughter Aanya over from Bangalore. Her heartfelt words made it all worth it.</p>
                    <p>This one was an ode to the Calcutta girl in her. To the fighter in her. To the Aparajita&nbsp;in&nbsp;her.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="pawan" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
