                                  <p>Like each year, the ‘Lifetime Achievement’ Jury Award for the 13th edition at Dhoot Group presents Sanmarg Aparajita 2024, powered by BMD Group and Bengal Energy Ltd. goes to a trailblazer whose life has been testament to her strength. Prof. Somdatta Sinha is a pioneering researcher and professor of Biology, and one of the first scientists in India to explore theoretical biology. Her 50 years of dedication have significantly advanced scientific understanding, particularly in protein structure and biochemical pathways. Her renowned research paper, “Mathematical Models of Malaria: A Review,” published in 2011, has over 500 citations. Currently, she studies the epidemiology of infectious diseases and the evolution of HIV-1. Professor Sinha’s work has not only improved the medical field but also inspired the new generation to&nbsp;pursue&nbsp;science.</p>
