                                  <p>To be brave you have to stand for what you believe in no matter what, and nobody knows this better than Dr. Tawheeda Makhdoomi. She hails from Jammu and Kashmir, and her work in the region has been brave and bold. A devoted child rights expert and academician holding a PhD from the University of Jammu, her work focuses on personality differentials among socially advantaged and disadvantaged adolescents in Kashmir. She serves as a resource person for IGNOU and is a past chair of the Child Welfare Committee in Anantnag, J&#038;K. She has also been teaching for 15 years. Further, she has extended her research to the mental health of socially disadvantaged half-widows and differently-abled persons in Kashmir. Dr. Tawheeda is a beacon of hope shining bright for at-risk persons in a vulnerable region. Dr. Makhdoomi is the recipient of the ‘Protector of Child Rights’ Jury Award at Dhoot Group presents Sanmarg Aparajita 2024, powered by BMD Group and Bengal Energy Ltd.</p>
