                    <p>At 11, Payal Jangid defied child marriage in her village of Heensla, Rajasthan. Twice elected Bal Sarpanch under the Bal Mitra Gram program, she helped 76 children return to school, stopped six child marriages, and fought for dignity and education. Her work has taken her to Sweden for the World’s Children’s Prize, earned her the Goalkeepers Award (2019) and Reebok’s “Fit to Fight” award, and global recognition as a youth leader. Now 21, she is pursuing a B.Ed., preparing for the Rajasthan Administrative Services, and teaching village children in her spare time.</p>
