               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
              <p>At 55, Ruby Pareek from Dausa, Rajasthan, has spent two decades transforming farming and lives. After losing her father to cancer, she turned to organic methods, determined to stop “feeding poison” to the next generation.
With NABARD’s support in 2006, Ruby expanded her work beyond her own fields, freely sharing earthworms, compost sprays, and techniques, especially with women. Her efforts not only improved farms but also gave women the courage to step beyond purdah and earn livelihoods.
From a single vermicomposting unit, her mission has reached over 26,000 people, including 11,000 women. Today at her Didwana center, she continues to grow more than crops—she nurtures dignity, empowerment, and faith in the soil itself.
</p>
