              <p>Since 2002, Aparajita Datta has worked in the forests of Arunachal Pradesh, discovering the Arunachal macaque, leading the first wildlife census, and helping tribes shift from hunting to education and healthcare. Author of 90+ publications and field guides, she has saved hornbills, and fought for the endangered leaf deer and black barking deer.
A wildlife ecologist with the Nature Conservation Foundation, she is a Whitley Award winner and Co-Chair of the IUCN Hornbill Specialist Group. In every hornbill’s return and every tree restored, her koshish lives on. Aparajita lives on.
