    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="ZAREEN" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">ZAREEN DESAI</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
              <p>A Le Cordon Bleu- trained chef and barista, Zareen is the founder of the popular Zee&#8217;s Coffeeshop in Ballygunge. Known for its hot chocolate, cold brew and curated events, Zee&#8217;s helps bring people together over music, community and coffee. She is also the founder of Bagan Farm, a family-run farm that helps deliver organic, top-quality seasonal produce throughout Bengal. Zareen also curates and hosts seasonal culinary experiences at Bagan, which doubles as a restaurant during the winter months. An interdisciplinary creative, she is  passionate about design and photography.
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="KAVITA" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">KAVITA KAJARIA</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
              <p>Kavita Kajaria is the founder of 8Finity Enterprises, a purpose-driven brand that transforms waste items into a range of stylish fashion and lifestyle products. Her organisation works with a wide variety of waste materials, using them as a base to create unique embellishments. The brand recently received India&#8217;s Best Product Design Award, honouring their commitment to sustainable innovation.  She has created a women-led team, employing skilled female artisans from marginalised communities. Further, she also leads Green Pari- an initiative which stitches and distributes cloth sanitary pads to women in underserved areas, promoting menstrual hygiene and well-being. She works extensively with Jal Pari- an organisation that has so far helped over 5 rural Bengali villages gain access to clean drinking water.
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="LATA" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">LATA BHATIA</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
              <p>Lata Bhatia began her zero-waste journey in 2016. She gradually moved away from disposables and adopted composting, recycling, and solar energy at home. Her kitchen waste feeds her terrace garden, and she follows a minimalist lifestyle. She ran a planned zero-waste store in Kolkata until recently and continues to advise organisations and raise awareness on sustainable living.
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="SRIYAM" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">SRIYAM MALL</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
              <p>As the co-founder and CEO of Hulladek Recycling, Sriyam Mall has spent nearly a decade pioneering how e-waste is managed across Eastern India. A global thinker and innovator, she has led Hulladek in championing a door-to-door e-waste collection process which extends to business organisations as well across India, ensuring the waste goes in for recycling. From ideating and piloting a new programme on plastic waste prevention to helping expand the business’s Extended Producer Responsibility segment, sustainability is at the forefront of all her work. Throughout her career, Sriyam has successfully fostered a culture of environmental stewardship and quietly driven change in communities across Eastern India. 
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
