                                    <p class="mb-4">A day of discovery. This is where the edition’s Aparajitas come together – as a family – for the first time. We call it&nbsp;the&nbsp;homecoming.</p>
                                    <p class="mb-4">The pre-event meet was a precursor to the main ceremony in Kolkata. It was held at ITC Pala on the 18th of July, 2024. It brought together the year&#8217;s council, the nominees as well as Aparajita honorees from past editions.</p> 
                                    <p class="mb-4">Since its inception, Aparajita endeavored not only to recognize outstanding women but also to foster a supportive ecosystem that encouraged their growth and impact. In its 10th edition, the awards took a bold step by employing women from the New Light Foundation as on-ground support, showcasing a commitment to inclusivity and empowerment beyond accolades.</p>
                                    <p class="mb-4">“We were thrilled to celebrate the stories of remarkable women through our new initiative to support rural women of West Bengal and Bihar. Aparajita was born out of a vision to highlight the journeys and achievements of women who have overcome immense challenges to make a difference. Much like Usain Bolt’s relentless pursuit of excellence, our awardees embody resilience and determination. Aparajita helps women by providing a platform to showcase their achievements, inspiring others, and fostering a supportive community for continued growth and empowerment. I believe that just like it takes a village to raise a child, similarly it takes a society to empower its women.” &#8211; Ruchika Gupta, President Sanmarg and Founder-Guardian Aparajita</p>
                                </div>
