                    <div class="modal fade" id="harpreet" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Harpreet Kaur Chandi</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>In 2024, Aparajita announces a historic first for us &#8211; presenting Polar Preet, our first international awardee. Harpreet Kaur Chandi aka Polar Preet is especially flying in from the UK to accept the Strength Jury Award at Dhoot Group presents Sanmarg Aparajita 2024, powered by BMD Group and Bengal Energy Ltd. With two Guinness World Records to her name, she is a physiotherapist and British Army medical officer originally from Punjab, who is renowned for being the first woman of colour to embark on a solo expedition to Antarctica. After dedicating over two years to rigorous training, Preet carried 90kg of weight daily and braved harsh temperatures to achieve this feat. She is also the published author of a children&#8217;s book, “The Explorer&#8217;s Guide to Going Wild: Find Adventure Anywhere,” inspiring Indian-origin women and children everywhere to break the glass ceiling.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="somdatta" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Prof. Somdatta Sinha</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>Like each year, the ‘Lifetime Achievement’ Jury Award for the 13th edition at Dhoot Group presents Sanmarg Aparajita 2024, powered by BMD Group and Bengal Energy Ltd. goes to a trailblazer whose life has been testament to her strength. Prof. Somdatta Sinha is a pioneering researcher and professor of Biology, and one of the first scientists in India to explore theoretical biology. Her 50 years of dedication have significantly advanced scientific understanding, particularly in protein structure and biochemical pathways. Her renowned research paper, “Mathematical Models of Malaria: A Review,” published in 2011, has over 500 citations. Currently, she studies the epidemiology of infectious diseases and the evolution of HIV-1. Professor Sinha’s work has not only improved the medical field but also inspired the new generation to pursue science.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="tawheeda" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">                
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Dr. Tawheeda Makhdoomi</h5>
                                   <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                  <p>To be brave you have to stand for what you believe in no matter what, and nobody knows this better than Dr. Tawheeda Makhdoomi. She hails from Jammu and Kashmir, and her work in the region has been brave and bold. A devoted child rights expert and academician holding a PhD from the University of Jammu, her work focuses on personality differentials among socially advantaged and disadvantaged adolescents in Kashmir. She serves as a resource person for IGNOU and is a past chair of the Child Welfare Committee in Anantnag, J&#038;K. She has also been teaching for 15 years. Further, she has extended her research to the mental health of socially disadvantaged half-widows and differently-abled persons in Kashmir. Dr. Tawheeda is a beacon of hope shining bright for at-risk persons in a vulnerable region. Dr. Makhdoomi is the recipient of the ‘Protector of Child Rights’ Jury Award at Dhoot Group presents Sanmarg Aparajita 2024, powered by BMD Group and Bengal Energy Ltd.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="modal fade" id="suman" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                            <div class="modal-content">
                                <div class="modal-header">
                                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Suman Jalan</h5>
                                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="modal-body">
                                    <p>As one of the leaders of industry in specialty steel production &amp; manufacturing, Bengal Energy has also pushed for sustainability &amp; the education of the underprivileged during her tenure. She has been associated with Aparajita for 4 years now and has lent her expertise in management &amp; critical insights through editions.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="aditi" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Aditi Murarka Agrawal</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Aditi seamlessly merges home decor with e-commerce, driving branding, marketing, and new product development since the brand&#8217;s inception in 2019. Under her leadership, Nestasia now supports over 150 artisans in Kolkata.She champions the Nestasia ArtJET Program, empowering artisans&#8217; children. The Designer Affiliate Program at Nestasia fosters collaborative growth in the design community. She has 5 offline retail stores, the first one being in Kolkata.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="aradhita" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Aradhita Agrawal</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Aradhita, a trailblazer in the tea industry, defied societal norms to become the sole manager of the family tea estates. Her legacy of entrepreneurship transitioned her smoothly into estate management, challenging the male-dominated sphere with her expertise in cultivation, manufacturing, and sales. Under her leadership, Karala Valley has risen to prominence, ranking among Bengal&#8217;s top 20 estates and transforming it’s reputation for quality tea production. She is also the co-founder of Chaika instant tea.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="snehja" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Snehja Sanganeria</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Snehja, with over 8 years of experience, excels in strategizing and delivering bespoke marketing solutions for diverse industries and client portfolios. Under her leadership, Meraqi Digital is the fastest-growing agency in the city. She is also a certified Face Yoga Specialist and Health Coach. Snehja is an advocate for financial literacy and freedom in women and encourages those on her team for the same.
                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="mona" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Monalisa Sarkar Mitra</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Her inner voice had always told her that she would be an artist. Raised in the hills amidst birdsong, she found inspiration in her surroundings from a young age. Now her love for nature and music shines through her art. She is dedicated to empowering women by teaching her crafts, initially from her home and now through her own art school and support for NGOs. Her mission is to foster a culture of growth and empowerment, encouraging women to pursue their passions and realize their dreams.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="shikha" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Shikha Chatterjee</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Shikha runs a ceramic studio in Burdwan, where she creates sculptures and crockery and also teaches the art. Her passion began in childhood and she specialized in Pottery and Ceramics at Banaras Hindi University (BHU). She wants to set up a production unit, to provide employment to women in rural and sub-urban areas and in turn support their families. She believes in sharing her knowledge to grow the art community and also provide avenues to others to become self reliant. </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="mina" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Mina Pandit</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>From her hands to the hearts of the likes of Rekha, Kapil Dev and the editors of Conde Nast Traveller &#8211; a third-generation puchkawali who fulfils out-of-station orders and supplies puchkas and puchka masala all over India, continuing her work even during the pandemic. She has educated her daughters just as much as her son and passed on her skills accrued over 45 years of working to her children, believing in self-sufficiency and hard work.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="katayun" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Katayun Saklat</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Katayun is the passionate stained glass painter behind Kolkata&#8217;s Fire Temple windows and
                founder of Gallery Katayun. With a rich career exploring themes from dreamscapes to Zoroastrianism. She is dedicated to advancing education for deaf children, advocating for the Parsi community, and promoting young artists. As one of India&#8217;s most accomplished stained glass designers, her work is part of several public and private collections. 
                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="mina" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Mina Pandit</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Under her aegis, The Indian Institute of Crafts and Design (IICD) Jaipur has flourished, as has The India Story, a flagship project of the Neotia Arts Trust. In 2010, Madhu took home the Aparajita for Healthcare for making specialised healthcare accessible for women &#038; children through the Bhagirathi Neotia Woman and Child Care Centre, and later joined us as jury member &#038; true steering force for Aparajita. She embodies every Aparajita that has graced our platform.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="soma" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Soma Das</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Fascinated by cooking from a young age, Soma is a self-taught chef who learned from
                cookbooks and newspaper recipes. She began catering with her aunt Vishakha and learnt the trade. She now employs her three sisters. Thirty years ago, she introduced Asian and Mexican cuisine to Kolkata. She generously teaches cooking to her neighbors and women seeking employment, often for free. She also offers
                a unique service of cooking in clients&#8217; homes.
                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="rangu" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Rangu Souriya</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Kanchanjungha Uddhar Kendra was founded in 2004 with Rangu’s savings and small donations from well-wishers at a time when the closures of tea gardens were causing spikes in the trafficking of women &#038; children. She. Her work has earned her numerous honors from both government and non-government organizations. She is renowned for her tireless efforts in combating human trafficking.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="nilima" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Nilima Ghosh</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Nakshi produces innovative and sustainable home décor, handloom and hand-crafted products, empowering rural artisans and supporting disabled individuals in the districts of West Bengal. Since its inception in 2012, Nilima personally looks into all administrative and functional aspects of Nakshi. She is also passionate about training the disabled artisans and supporting them with employment opportunities, through her dedicated endeavours.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="rup" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Ruplekha Sinha Roy</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>A Buddhist practitioner, certified Montessori teacher, Heal Your Life coach, and counselor. She holds degrees from Lawrence School Sanawar, Sophia College for Women, and a Ph.D. in teaching from IEA. Her journey with Lotus Rescue began with three street children and has expanded to serving 1,000 children and 380 women in West Bengal through projects like ‘Shikhshayatan’ and ‘Nari Saksham’ whereas ‘Vishnupriya’ empowers 25 transgender individuals. She stays at Sunderbans every week to accomplish her vision personally.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="modal fade" id="temit" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
                        <div class="modal-content">
                            <div class="modal-header">                
                                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Temit Lepcha</h5>
                               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="modal-body">
                              <p>Temit moved to Kolkata from Kalimpong in 1986. She specialises in cooking authentic Chinese food including momos. Crossing language barriers and with no education, she is an example of grit and passion. She is a keeper of the cultural food tradition specific to Calcutta  &#8211; of women serving steaming hot breakfasts of authentic Chinese food at Tiretta Bazaar (Chinatown) on weekends. Temit lives all by herself and plays an active role in the community by running errands for the elderly in her neighborhood.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
