        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Dr. Neerja Rateria</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Dr. Neerja Rateria has spent the last five decades restoring the eyesight of her patients even in the most dire of situations.<br><br>
After completing her studies in 1965, Dr. Rateria began practicing Ophthalmology at SSKM Hospital. Thereafter, she became associated with multiple organizations including North Bengal University and Ramakrishna Mission before becoming a private practitioner.<br><br>
Now retired, Neerja has also traveled extensively to Nigeria for eye camps organised
for the treatment of the marginalised section of people there.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="reenaNair" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Dr. Reena Nair</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Dr. Reena Nair is a Senior Consultant in Clinical Hematology and heads the Department of Medical Oncology at Tata Medical Centre, Kolkata. She completed her MBBS and MD from Goa Medical College. Subsequently she did Medical Oncology Residency and Fellowship at Tata Memorial Hospital before becoming a Medical Oncology Faculty [Lecturer to Professor] at Tata Memorial Hospital, Mumbai. She is the Founding member of the Lymphoma Registry of Mumbai. Her current interest is in management of Hematological malignancies and she has published over 125 papers and book chapters. She was recently Honoured at the Doctors Conclave award of the Economic Times in the category of ‘Inspiring Oncologist of India’.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="sushmitaRoyChowdhury" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Dr. Sushmita Roy Chowdhury</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Dr. Sushmita Roy Chowdhury is an expert pulmonologist with an experience of  20 years. After completing her MBBS in 1997, she pursued MD in Tuberculosis &#038; Respiratory Diseases/Medicine and MRCP (UK). Dr. Sushmita Roy specializes in Pulmonology, Sleep Medicine and Allergy and is currently the Director at Fortis Hospital Anandapur, Kolkata.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="ashwikaKapur" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Ashwika Kapur</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Ashwika Kapur is a qualified Science Communicator and an International Award-winning Wildlife &#038; Nature Filmmaker. She became India’s youngest and only woman to win a ‘Green Oscar’ or a Panda Award in a global category.<br><br> 
She has also been awarded at New York Wild Film Festival, and named a Grand Teton Finalist at Jackson Wild, USA. Over the years, she&#8217;s worked on programmes for various platforms such as Animal Planet, Discovery, Netflix and BBC, her most recent projects being Attenborough&#8217;s Life in Colour and Planet Defenders. She is currently working on a Tiger conservation  documentary. Her climate change and biodiversity documentation work in the Sundarbans, was showcased at the United Nations Climate Change Conference (COP26) in November 2021 in Glasgow.<br><br> 
She is also a professional public speaker and passionate nature educator, regularly delivering wildlife &#038; conservation talks to thousands of students and young people in India &#038; UK to inspire young minds to champion the cause of conservation.
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="mamoniChitrakar" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Mamoni Chitrakar</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Trained by her mother since childhood, Mamoni Chitrakar, has been painting on Pata scrolls and singing Pata songs. She specializes in paintings on Manasha Mangal and Chandi Mangal. Besides mastering the art of painting mythological characters and stories, Mamoni has also painted on issues of social concern to spread awareness and commemorate tragedies like 9/11 and natural disasters such as tsunamis and floods, social and health education.<br><br>
She has showcased her art across India. Internationally, her art has taken her to Italy, Paris, Washington and Bahrain in fairs, exhibitions and spaces of cultural exchange. She has participated in multiple cultural exchange programs with Smithsonian Centre for Folklife and Cultural Heritage and visited Smithsonian Folklife Festival 2018 in Washington, D.C. She has also performed at cultural institutions like at the Freer Sackler Gallery.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="sangitaMaity" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Sangita Maity</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>A freelance visual artist by profession, Sangita Maity focuses on issues of labour, occupational migration and related socio-cultural and environmental issues faced by the marginalised section of the society. Her work represents their situations in visual forms.<br><br>
Following several years of engagement with the Barbil iron ore mines, one of India&#8217;s largest of its kind located in the Keonjhar district of Orissa, she is now working with communities that revolve around rubber plantations in Tripura.<br><br> 
Maity has received Junior Fellowship from Ministry of Culture, 2018 -2019 &#038; CIMA Jury Award 2015. She has participated in Khoj Peers Residency at Khoj Artists Association in New Delhi. Sangita has presented a solo show at Clark House Initiative, Mumbai in 2018. She was part of the show ‘Look, Stranger!’ Curated by Rahaab Allana for Serendipity Art Festival 2019. She has exhibited in Dr. Bhau Daji Lad Museum, Mumbai in 2016. She has exhibited in Hub India at Artissima in Turin Italy and Museo Camera in Gurgaon, 2021.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="eshaChatterjee" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Esha Chatterjee</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Esha Chatterjee is the <b>Founder and CEO of BEE Books</b>, a Kolkata based English Publishing House.<br><br> 
BEE Books publishes everything from translations, fiction, non-fiction, essays to graphic novels and corporate coffee table books. Esha is also the Managing Director of ‘Patra Bharati’ and heads the marketing wing for the Bengali publishing press.<br><br>
Her biggest challenge as the Founder of BEE Books was to establish an English publishing house in Kolkata and earn recognition for the same.<br><br>
Esha is also a book reviewer, critic and moderator for literary events and has been associated with a number of literature festivals.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="roshniAditya" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Roshni Aditya</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Roshni Aditya, the Managing Director of Aditya Group has the primary role of controlling and directing the company’s resources and looking into the retention and recruitment of the required workforce.
She is an integral part of the Managing Committee of Bhaskar Aditya Foundation and the Dum Dum Aditya Educational Society. She directs and supervises the activities of the principals and the Board to ensure all of the efforts are in alignment with strategies for attaining goals. Roshni is in charge of the day-to-day operations at Noodle Oodle, an authentic Asian cuisine restaurant chain, is responsible for its performance and constantly working to develop new ideas.<br><br>
A leader and strategist, she has been able to steer the company in the most profitable direction while ensuring the company’s vision and long-term goals are met. She has successfully built and managed a diverse group of employees and led them towards achieving growth in a competitive and dynamic environment.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="niveditaPoddar" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
