        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Nivedita Poddar</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Nivedita Poddar is the founder and creative director of Art Fervour, India’s first visual arts discovery platform. Art Fervour positions itself as India&#8217;s art &#038; tech platform that makes arts accessible to all. <br><br> 
Apart from Art Fervour, Nivedita was also instrumental in bringing Gurr Johns, one of the world’s leading art valuations &#038; advisory companies to India.<br><br>  
Prior to starting Art Fervour and working with Gurr Johns India, Nivedita was a Gallery Associate for Experimenter Gallery&#8217;s participation in Frieze London in 2015.<br><br> 
She holds a Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration and Management and a Master’s Degree from Christie’s Education, London in Modern and Contemporary Art: Art History and Art World Practices. Nivedita is also a digital strategist for the arts and a self-taught independent photographer.
</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="aninditaMajumdar" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Anindita Majumdar</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Anindita Majumdar is the <b>Founder and Managing Trustee of  Equidiversity Foundation</b> and is a Gender Consultant with a number of NGOs.<br><br>
Having worked against Gender Based Violence for more than two decades, she got nominated under the prestigious International Leadership Programme (IVLP) 2014 and became an Ashoka Fellow in 2017.<br><br> 
With widespread support from women in the community, and Gram Panchayats, coupled with the determination shown by some of her previous team members, an extremely motivated Anindita started the Equidiversity Foundation on 15 September, 2016 as a Charitable Trust. The aim of her work is to change the Gram Panchayats in West Bengal’s rural governance system from one where women serve as proxy leaders to one where women actively participate in decision-making processes &#038; governing, ensuring democratic leadership. Besides working with women elected representatives (WER) of Gram Panchayat, her foundation also works with systems to cultivate and nurture future democratic, gender sensitive and inclusive leadership.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="roopaMehta" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Roopa Mehta</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Roopa Mehta, the <b>Co-founder and CEO of Sasha Fair Trade</b> has been working in the area of craft and textile development and promotion for the past four decades.<br><br>
Back in 1978, with the advent of machine-made goods, craft began to suffer. Artisans, especially women were increasingly being marginalized by middlemen and their products trivialized as either ethnic or purely decorative. Sasha was founded to address these issues and empower artisans.<br><br>
Currently the President of the World Fair Trade Organization (WFTO) and one of the former Presidents of Fair Trade Forum &#8211; India, Roopa&#8217;s work at Sasha is guided by fair trade principles, committing to create sustainable livelihoods for the handloom and handicraft sector.<br><br>
In her own words, &#8220;Deep enduring passion for our rich traditional handloom textiles developed in time and grew with further understanding of the skills and the entire weaving process. The challenge is to make handlooms more visible and accessible, generating a sense of pride in what is our cultural identity.&#8221;</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="sarbaniDas" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Sarbani Das Roy</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Sarbani Das Roy is the <b>Co-founder &#038; Director of Iswar Sankalpa</b>. Her organisation lends a helping hand to those with mental health problems, particularly those from underprivileged sections of the society. <br><br>
She also runs a shelter named <b>Sarbari</b> for abandoned, mentally ill women and has helped more than 200 such women unite with their families. She identifies the homeless, connects them with government institutions and gets them treated, while continuing to work on their social acceptance.<br><br>
Sarbani runs a mainstream cafe managed by people with psychosocial disabilities and dreams of setting up an independent living facility for uprooted women and food kiosks run by people with mental illnesses. </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="anubhaFatehpuria" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Anubha Fatehpuria</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Anubha Fatehpuria – actor (since 1995) &#038; architect (since 2001) – is recipient of the Sangeet Natak Akademi’s Ustad Bismillah Khan Yuva Puruskar 2013-14, The Telegraph SHE Awards 2019 and Shyamal Sen Smriti Puraskar 2007 for her theatre acting.<br><br>
She has worked with directors like Habib Tanveer, Shyamanand Jalan, Usha Ganguli, Rajinder Nath, Alyque Padamsee, Wlodzimierz Staniewski, Suman Mukhopadhyay, Vinay Sharma, Vikarm Iyengar, John Britton, Purva Naresh – to name some.<br><br>
She received extensive theatre training from Late Shyamanand Jalan. She continues to learn the craft of theatre-making under director Vinay Sharma from 2006 onwards. <br><br>
Anubha is currently also Director-Programmes at Padatik Theatre.<br><br>
Her screen directors have been  Seema Pahwa, Prasoon Pandey, Aparna Sen, Shoojit Sircar, Aniruddha Roy Chowdhury, Atul Mongia, Laxman Utekar &#8211; to name some. <br><br>
Anubha is trained in Hindustani Vocal, Bharatnatyam, Visual Arts, Martial Arts under stalwarts like Late Girija Devi, Mitali Sengupta, Thankamani Kutty, Arup Das &#8211; to name a few. <br><br>
A Gold Medallist from Nagpur University for Bachelors in Architecture, Anubha worked under Ar. B.V. Doshi and Ar. Dulal Mukherjee briefly.<br><br>
Her design studio has received several recognitions for green practices.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="shashwatiGarai" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="exampleModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog  modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">                
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Shashwati Garai Ghosh</h5>
               <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">X</button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">              
              <p>Shashwati Garai Ghosh, a trained dancer, teacher and choreographer in the Odissi dance form of Indian Classical dance, began receiving Odishi lessons in 1999 under the tutelage of eminent dancer-choreographer Smt Sharmila Biswas. She has received special training from legends such as Guru Kelucharan Mohapatra, Smt Kalanidhi Narayanan, Smt Sonal Mansingh, and Shri Durgacharan Ranbir. Dr Kannan Pughazendi also provided her with dance medicine and fitness training. She holds an MA in Odissi dance from Rabindra Bharati University in Kolkata.<br><br>
She owns and operates her own dance school, Angashuddhi, in Kolkata, and conducts regular workshops for schools and institutions throughout India and abroad. She has toured extensively in India and abroad, both with the Odissi Vision and Movement Center ensemble and on her own, giving notable performances at prestigious festivals.<br><br>
Many awards, accolades, and fellowships have been bestowed upon Shashwati throughout her career, including the Ustad Bismillah Khan Yuva Puraskar, Guru Kelucharan Mohapatra Yuva Pratibha Samman (first recipient), Sanskriti-Madhobi Chatterjee Memorial Fellowship, Kalavaahini Senior Fellowship, Nalanda Nritya Nipuna Award, Odissi Jyoti Award, Shringar Man.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
